---
import {KOBO_APPS} from '../../lib/kobo-contract.mjs';
import Settings from '../../layouts/Settings.astro';
import {protectPage} from '../../../server/identity';
export const prerender=false;
const access=await protectPage('/studio/storage');if(access instanceof Response)return access;
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control','private, no-store');
---

<Settings title="Files & storage settings" section="storage">
<section class="settings-section"><h2>Files & storage</h2><p>One set of storage connections for all your apps. Your private files and connections stay associated with your account.</p><div class="storage-destination"><label for="save-destination">Default save destination</label><select id="save-destination"><option value="download">Download to this device</option><option value="site">Private site storage</option><option value="webdav">My WebDAV folder</option></select><button type="button" id="save-preferences" class="btn">Save preference</button></div><p>Each export still asks you to save. A device folder is controlled by your browser, rather than stored on your account.</p><p id="preference-status" role="status"></p></section>
<section class="settings-section"><div class="connection-heading"><h2>WebDAV</h2><span class="connection-badge">File connection</span></div><p>Connect your existing HTTPS WebDAV account. Kōbō uses a separate folder for each app; the current editors can also copy exports to this connection.</p><p id="storage-status" role="status">Checking connection…</p><details class="connection-details"><summary>Connection details</summary><form id="webdav-form" class="form" method="post" action="/api/storage/webdav"><label>Connection name<input name="label" maxlength="120" placeholder="My kDrive" /></label><label>WebDAV account/folder URL<input name="url" type="url" placeholder="https://cloud.example.com/remote.php/dav/files/username/Explore/" required /></label><label>Kōbō base folder<input name="baseFolder" value="Kobo" placeholder="Kobo" /><small>Relative to the URL above. Hikari uses Kobo/Hikari. Leave blank if the URL already ends in /Kobo/.</small></label><label>Username<input name="username" autocomplete="username" required /></label><label>App password<input name="password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" required /></label><div class="connection-actions"><button class="btn" type="submit">Test & save</button><button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="webdav-remove">Disconnect</button></div></form><p>The test writes and removes a temporary file. Your app password is encrypted and is never returned to this form.</p></details><h3>Experimental Kōbō sync</h3><p>After connecting, test conditional saves, metadata, read-back and safe deletion. This creates temporary files under the Hikari folder. Passing this connection check does not complete the app’s full acceptance tests.</p><button type="button" id="verify-kobo" disabled>Test Kōbō sync connection</button><p id="kobo-verification" role="status">First enter your connection details and complete Test & save.</p></section>
<section class="settings-section"><div class="connection-heading"><h2>Google Drive</h2><span class="connection-badge">Experimental Kōbō sync</span></div><p>Connect a Google account to use a dedicated Kōbō folder. This permission covers files created or opened with this integration; it does not grant access to your whole Drive. Google sign-in is separate.</p><p id="google-drive-status" role="status">Checking Google Drive…</p><div class="connection-actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="google-drive-connect" disabled>Connect Google Drive</button><button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="google-drive-verify" hidden>Test connection</button><button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="google-drive-disconnect" hidden>Disconnect</button><a id="google-drive-folder" hidden target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Kōbō folder ↗</a></div><p>Working revisions are kept as separate private files. Removing an app file removes its current reference; older cloud copies are retained. Disconnecting keeps your Drive files.</p>{access.isOwner&&<p id="google-drive-setup" hidden>Administrator setup is needed. See <a href="https://github.com/cuteclaudia/explore/blob/main/docs/GOOGLE-DRIVE-SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Drive setup instructions</a>. Keep your existing storage encryption key.</p>}</section>
<section class="settings-section"><h2>Google Drive recovery</h2><p>Automatic private index snapshots are saved before library heads are published. They preserve the mapping to your Drive files; they do not contain the photographs themselves. Keep your original files and app library backups too.</p><details><summary>Back up or recover the private index</summary><p>Close your apps before making a recovery checkpoint or restoring one. Restore verifies the saved Drive files, then activates a separate index. The previous index and cloud files are retained. A restore returns the selected app to the snapshot’s saved state.</p><label>App <select id="index-app">{Object.entries(KOBO_APPS).filter(([,spec])=>access.permissions[spec.capability]).map(([id,spec])=><option value={id}>{spec.folder}</option>)}</select></label><div class="connection-actions"><button type="button" id="index-refresh">Refresh snapshots</button><button type="button" id="index-capture">Create checkpoint</button></div><label>Saved index <select id="index-snapshot"><option value="">Refresh to load snapshots</option></select></label><div class="connection-actions"><button type="button" id="index-download" disabled>Download encrypted backup</button><button type="button" id="index-begin" disabled>Verify for restore</button></div><label>Import an encrypted index backup<input type="file" id="index-upload" accept=".json,application/json" /></label><p>Downloads are encrypted and tied to this website account and Drive connection. Recovery also needs the website’s original storage encryption key; keep a separate secure administrator copy of that key.</p><div class="connection-actions"><button type="button" id="index-pause" hidden>Pause verification</button><button type="button" id="index-resume" hidden>Resume verification</button><button type="button" id="index-publish" hidden>Activate restored index</button><button type="button" id="index-cancel" hidden>Cancel recovery</button></div><p id="index-status" role="status">Your Drive connection must be available to back up or restore its index.</p></details></section>
<section class="settings-section"><h2>Kōbō sync destination</h2><p>Choose a connected, verified provider for the new apps. Changing this does not copy or migrate a library. Existing export preferences above are separate.</p><label for="kobo-provider">Active provider</label><select id="kobo-provider"><option value="webdav">WebDAV</option><option value="google-drive">Google Drive</option></select><button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="kobo-provider-save">Use this provider</button><p id="kobo-provider-status" role="status"></p></section>
<section class="settings-section"><h2>Other file providers</h2><p>OneDrive integration is planned. For services without a supported web integration, you can download exports to a folder managed by their desktop sync app.</p></section>
{access.isOwner&&<details class="admin-storage"><summary>Administrator setup</summary><p>First time only: generate a key for FILE_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY in Netlify. Keep an existing key unchanged to preserve saved connection credentials.</p><button type="button" id="generate-storage-key" class="btn ghost">Generate setup key</button><label>New encryption key<input id="storage-key" type="password" readonly autocomplete="off" /></label><button type="button" id="copy-storage-key" class="btn ghost">Copy key</button></details>}
</Settings>
<script>import '../../scripts/storage-settings';import '../../scripts/storage-index-recovery';</script>
<style>.storage-destination{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0 10px}.connection-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}.connection-heading h2{margin:0}.connection-badge{font-size:11px;opacity:.6}.connection-details summary,.admin-storage summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;padding:12px 0}.connection-details form{max-width:580px;margin-top:15px}.connection-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}#index-snapshot{max-width:100%}#index-upload{display:block;margin-block:10px}.settings-section button:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:not-allowed}#kobo-verification[data-state=error],#storage-status[data-state=error]{opacity:1;color:var(--accent);font-weight:500}.admin-storage{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:5px 18px}.admin-storage input{display:block;width:100%;margin:10px 0}.admin-storage button{margin:8px 8px 8px 0}</style>
